- Keyboard shortcut to UNCOMMENT single or
multiple lines in an XML file - CTRL + SHIFT + \ -->

 <!--  1. Always create the testNG.xml file under src/test/resources folder 
	because src/main/java and src/test/java folders are meant to include only 
	the JAVA code 
	
	2. Testng runner file is needed because: 
	- We want to get rid 
	of the burden of running each test class separately 
	- We want to generate 
	a single report for all the test classes at once (not running them separately) 
	- We want to see the failures for all the test classes in a single run and 
	single report not by running test classes separately
	
	3. Verbose keyword is used to define the level of logs generated by testNG in the console. More
	the value of Verbose more detailed logs will be generated in the console. For very minimum Verbose value too
	few logs will be generated and for very large Verbose value too detailed logs will be generated
	
	4. The minimum value of Verbose keyword is 1 and maximum value is 10 
	
	5. Thread-count variable is used to give the number of threads that are going to
	    be initiated for all the test cases to run
	6. Parallel keyword is used to define what to run in parallel mode tests or classes
	    where tests are equivalent to the <test> tag and classes are equivalent
	    to the <class> tag given in the testNG runner file.
    7. Thread-count is not always equal to the number of browsers to be launched for test cases.
        For e.g. if we have 10 test cases then we can give thread-count as 5.
    8. But we should use the thread-count value very wisely. For e.g. if 
        we have only 3 tests then giving 10 thread-count is unnecessary because
       maximum 3 threads can be used to perform testing for all the 3 tests at the same time.
       Then remaining 7 threads will be wasted and unnecessary occupy the memory. 
       Whereas if we have 50 tests then giving 50 threads will be very costly operation because
       then system will try to consume max. threads at the same time i.e. 50 and it will 
       launch 50 browsers at the same time which will put huge amount of load on system's memory
       and it will crash.
       So, the strategy could be 3 threads for 3 tests and 5 threads for 50 tests.
       For 3 threads testNG will launch all 3 tests' browser at the same time consuming 3 threads.
       For 5 threads testNG will launch 5 tests' browser in a group at the same time consuming 5 threads and
       likewise it will execute group of 5 browser 10 times. 
    9. We can use the parameter tag in the runner file to use different parameters while running
    out tests like which browesr to run tests, which environment to run tests etc.
    10.  Generally we create different xml/runner files to run the tests
    on different browsers -->
	

<suite name="TestNG Regression Suite" thread-count = "4"  parallel = "tests" verbose="4">

